##  V4: June 26, 2024
##  1. Add argument-count to operators
##  2. Add operator-action-map so can have two rules for external action execution [since removed]
##  3. Added search-control (optional) for avoiding undoing actions (close after open for example). 
##  4. Eliminated transformation search control because #3 is more natural.
##  5. SVS substates disabled.
##
### Version V3:
##  Modifies V2:
##   1. in-container -> in x
##   2. on-location -> on x
##   3. count -> desired-count x
##   4. add argument-count to in and on relations  x
##   5. add argument-count to operator <---
##   6. Change all operator and relation arguments to argument1 (usually the object being manipulated) and argument2. x
##   7. Modify rules to take advantage of this. x
##   8. Start to address comments below.
##
##  Experimental Version with Rosie State/object representations.
##    laird-thor-soar without V2 is the original that this was copied from.
##    moved mutable features from world model into objects.
##  1. Modified datamap by adding true/false attributes to ^object; removed corresponding attributes from ^world
##  2. Operator by operator, moved those features. 3:02pm;  cook finished at 3:45pm (43min) cook substate finished 4:30pm (45 min); break-object 4:45 (15 min); close 5:07 (22min) 
##     open 5:33 (26 min); get-object (19 min); go-to (18 min)

## Comments
## A. Before, all desireds were attributes of the world. Now, many are attributes of an object. Need
## B. In new - if have multiple properties of an object, hard to represent? Must create new object with properties copied?  In cooking, next to the closed object being used to cook. 
##   - create a new object with the handle - doesn't have all properties. with a duplicate-of pointer?  Will copy in substate?
## C. Holding needs to be thought through. Might be on object and on world. Maybe a relation between self and an object. Need to know if not holding anything (none). Easier if relation - don't have to test for absence of holding on all objects.
## D. Type graspable should be graspable true - did it...
## E. Looks like get-object can have just one external pickup !!!!!
## F. Unsure about go - why a separate mea proposal for a closed container - why preconditions achieved by has a desired to open container. !!!!!!  Other Changes!!!
## G. apply*go-to*internal*object-on-location1 - not clear object on a location should be reachable  !!!
## H. possible error in slice-object - all relations in proposal don't point to same object. !!
## J. Added elaborations for false values of activatable; breakable; cookable; fillable;  
## K. Needed to add sliceable (added all); toggle (haven't added...)
## L. !!! Need to check if thor-soar*elaborate*state*unacheived-desired is necessary !!!
## M. Fill-object external doesn't bind the <liquid> in the condition apply*fill-object*external
## N. No way to empy hand via MEA - should through put-on or put-in.

